From: Elevator HMI project <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: backport the whole subsystem from Boardcon rkr5 BSP

BLK-015: KMS scanout never latches on this board. Measured on target with
rockchipdrm debug=9 (VOP_DEBUG_PLANE | VOP_DEBUG_CFG_DONE), during a 4 s
modetest run: 241 plane updates and 243 cfg_done writes, paired 1:1, every
frame at 60 Hz:

    vp1 update Smart1-win0[800x1280@(0,0)->800x1280@(0,0)] fmt[XR24] addr[0x3e8000]
    cfg_done: 0x8002
    vp1 update Smart1-win0[800x1280@(0,0)->800x1280@(0,0)] fmt[XR24] addr[0x7d0000]
    cfg_done: 0x8002

0x8002 = RK3568_VOP2_GLB_CFG_DONE_EN | BIT(1) — the correct VP1 latch trigger
(the driver documents that RK3568 VP config-done bits carry no write mask). So
the driver programs the address and fires the latch correctly every frame, and
the hardware keeps scanning the buffer latched at boot. Only writes into that
buffer via /dev/fb0 ever reach the glass.

That rules out our DTS and our userspace, and points at the driver itself.
meta-rockchip pins a linux-rockchip that is NOT Boardcon's BSP for this board:

    drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
        ours  (meta-rockchip pin) : 423258 bytes
        Boardcon em3566 rkr5      : 451378 bytes   (2025-03-11)

A 3541-line diff in that file alone, with 28 functions present only in the
vendor driver, including:
  - vop2_handle_post_buf_empty + rate limiter (VOP2 display FIFO underrun IRQ;
    we have no handler at all)
  - vop2_set_aclk_rate (our DTB carries rockchip,aclk-normal-mode-rates but our
    driver has no code to consume it)
  - vop2_iommu_fault_handler
The vendor also ships its own rockchip_drm_fbdev.c, which our tree lacks
entirely (we use the generic DRM fbdev helper) — and fbdev is precisely the one
path that works here.

This replaces drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/ wholesale with the version from
    library/EM3566/Linux6.1/Source/em3566_linux6.1-rkr5-20250509.tar.bz2
rather than cherry-picking, because the files share headers and structs and a
partial backport would mix two ABIs.

EXCLUDED: rockchip_panel_notifier.c. It needs <linux/rockchip-panel-notifier.h>,
which lives outside this directory. It is gated by CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_PANEL_NOTIFIER
(no Kconfig default, and we pin it off in elevator-hmi.cfg).

Two other vendor includes are non-issues: <asm/dma-iommu.h> is inside
#if defined(CONFIG_ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU) (never true on arm64), and <drm/drmP.h> is
included by files present in BOTH trees that our config does not compile.

Panel patches 0001-0021 touch drivers/gpu/drm/panel/ and are unaffected.

NOT YET CONFIRMED to fix BLK-015. Kill test after flashing:
    modetest -M rockchip -s <connector>@<crtc>:800x1280
A visible test pattern means KMS scanout works, and the linuxfb/software-decode
detour can be unwound (EGLFS + Mali + VPU video).

Source: Boardcon EM3566 v3 BSP, em3566_linux6.1-rkr5-20250509, GPL-2.0.

NOTE ON GENERATION: an earlier attempt at this patch failed to apply because it
was diffed while build/tmp/work-shared/.../kernel-source happened to be checked
out at a different commit mid-do_patch (one carrying Rockchip's
"HACK: Force enable legacy-cursor-update", 5e63776cf6b0, which is NOT an
ancestor of the branch we build). The shared tree is therefore not a stable diff
base. This patch is generated against the clean post-do_patch tree and verified
with `git apply --check`.

Signed-off-by: Elevator HMI project <noreply@example.com>
---
